> But monsters never actually unlock anything, do they?

Monsters will unlock doors, but not containers. (They won't even loot
unlocked or unlockable containers, for that matter.) They will only
use skeleton keys, though, not credit cards; and they won't pick
skeleton keys up, so the only case this really matters is for
shopkeepers (who are created with them) and monsters that steal
objects from you (yes, even monkeys are intelligent enough to unlock a
door). Furthermore, the Wizard and the Riders have the magical ability
to unlock doors even without a key.

